{% import 'dashboard/_macros.html.twig' as ui %}
<p>Send a test message to a few addresses <strong>you own</strong> (for example one at Gmail and one at Outlook) and follow every stage. It goes out only when delivery is LIVE;
in HELD mode the job waits at "Claimed by the delivery daemon" — that itself shows the safety is working. {{ ui.help('sending') }}</p>
<p>Delivery is <span class="mode mode-{{ delivery.mode }}">{{ delivery.mode }}</span>.</p>
{% if clients is empty %}<p class="warn">No active client has a verified sending domain yet. Create a client for your own tests, add and verify its sending domain, and give it a DKIM key (step 7).</p>{% else %}
<form method="post" action="{{ path('dashboard_operator_setup_test_start') }}" class="stack">{{ ui.csrf() }}<input type="hidden" name="kind" value="seed">
    <label>Send as client <select name="client">{% for c in clients %}<option value="{{ c.id }}">{{ c.company_name }} ({{ c.domains }})</option>{% endfor %}</select></label>
    <label>From address (at one of that client's verified domains) <input name="sender_email" type="email" required></label>
    <label>Your addresses (1 to 5, separated by spaces) <textarea name="addresses" rows="2" required></textarea></label>
    <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" name="i_own_these" value="1" required> I own or control every one of these mailboxes.</label>
    <button type="submit">Send the seed test</button>
</form>{% endif %}
<p>After it arrives: show images (to record the open) and click the link (to record the click), then confirm below what you see in the message's headers.</p>
{% include 'dashboard/operator/setup/steps/_test_reports.html.twig' %}
